 {
  "claim_id": "C-019",
  "statement": "At the training learning rate, a Picbreeder start leaves at least twice the remaining edit error of a fully fitted dense network after 2000 steps, on skull and butterfly.",
  "scope": "phase0/continual_v2.py at 2000 steps, 64x64, same edits and optimizer as C-011 to C-018, learning rate stated per check. R is remaining error toward the new target, relative to the edit's size; its normalization does not depend on the network. Only fully fitted networks: PBd, PBa, G0. Written after seeing the earlier continual-learning results, so these are remeasurements with informed predictions, not blind tests. Picbreeder is one network per task and its edits are not independent samples, so results describe these networks and do not generalize to Picbreeder networks. Medians are descriptive. R at a fixed step needs no censoring.",
  "group": "PBd",
  "flip_boundary": "Learning rate may reverse this, which C-020 tests. Apple is left out: earlier results showed both groups near 0.22 of E0 there on local edits.",
